  "correct": "2",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nPrincipal (P) = ₹20,000\n\nRate (r) = 9%\n\nTime (t) = 2 years\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nA = P(1+(r)/(100))^t\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nA = 20000(1+(9)/(100))²\n\n⇒ A = 20000(1+0.09)²\n\n⇒ A = 20000(1.09)²\n\n⇒ A = 20000(1.1881)\n\n⇒ A = 20000 × 1.1881\n\n⇒ A = 23762\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (2).**",
